sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-018> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-018-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-018-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-018 — Plateau tri-junction (120 degree) claim: Lami balance, periodic froth relaxation, junction-angle statistics — MorphoEval overall 40.2/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 1 (v1) evaluation (overall 40.2/100). The baseline implements Lami balance with Thompson's three Fig. 113 cases, the Steiner-vs-cross inequality, the angle-sum identity statistics, and a periodic Voronoi froth relaxed under a Farhadifar-type energy at a single parameter point (relaxed junction-angle SD 19.0 deg vs 29.5 deg for the Voronoi seed), with a 3-panel figure and a relaxation GIF. It does NOT load, SHA-256-verify, or segment any of the four vendored specimens, does not sweep tension anisotropy or the partition-tension ratio, has no negative/ablation control beyond the unrelaxed seed, computes no goodness-of-fit, writes no result.json, and its froth relaxation is unconverged (SD 19 deg is far from the Plateau limit) because perimeter contractility makes edge tensions unequal and no T1 exchanges are allowed. Overall 40.2/100 (faithfulness 33.1, reproducibility 56.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 88f1e6cf4; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0, scikit-image 0.26.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 55, Morphological realism / specimen match 18, Parameter expressivity 32, Morphometric validation 30, Source and data traceability 58, Code-to-model traceability 62, Reproducibility package 52. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_018_the_forms_of_tissues_or_cell_a_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-018_the-forms-of-tissues-or-cell-aggregates.py at 88f1e6cf4, image/png, 180777 B, 1650×528 px, artifact_sha256 694426affc0cfe18c129d7d5186fc49be89908622078bab6eca93eb65d214765 (sha256 694426affc0cfe18c129d7d5186fc49be89908622078bab6eca93eb65d214765), spec_fingerprint 19f6f11c004310d9d3822d28b8f9f71011ff87e8a31986733b91a36effb75d46. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 19f6f11c004310d9d3822d28b8f9f71011ff87e8a31986733b91a36effb75d46; artifact_sha256: 694426affc0cfe18c129d7d5186fc49be89908622078bab6eca93eb65d214765; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-018/allium_cepa_epidermis_specimen.jpg=12d2cff76378adae..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-018/human_corneal_endothelium_specimen.jpg=9daed5fb546e11bf..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-018/ongrowthform1917thom_0318.jp2=fb329d9ddbe640d8..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-018/ongrowthform1917thom_0341.jp2=38d6d1a9bc86ad90..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-018/paper_citations.bib=ef63468ff8403071..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-018/scout_manifest.json=50b930d12b0f97e0..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-018/t1917_018_the_forms_of_tissues_or_cell_a_reference.json=213d7c371e7f98fe..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-018/thompson1917_fig103_maize_parenchyma.png=d1c3c3aa92d21321..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-018/thompson1917_fig124_girardia_epidermis.png=3a33c7b1b82aad70...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Thompson (1917) p. 297: three similar liquid surfaces always meet at 120 degrees; p. 303 Fig. 113 cases (1)-(3): 90 / >90 / 120 degrees as the partition tension t rises to T; p. 309-310: Lamarle's least-area partition meets in threes at 120 degrees, and 'in any ordinary section of a vegetable parenchyma ... cell-walls everywhere meeting, by threes, at angles of 120 degrees, irrespective of the size of the individual cells'. | Thompson (1917) pp. 314, 321-322: epidermal outer walls and growth/traction anisotropy (Fig. 124 Girardia) are stated exceptions where the angles depart from 120 degrees.; reconstructed_in_script: Lami/Neumann triangle of forces (E1) with Fig. 113 cases, Steiner-vs-cross film lengths (E2), angle-sum identity statistics (E3), and a periodic Poisson-Voronoi vertex network relaxed by gradient descent on a Farhadifar-type energy (E5) at one parameter point.; transfer_boundary: 2D plane section / en-face projection of a 3D cell aggregate; Thompson's 109 deg 28' tetrahedral edge law is not simulated.; does_not_claim: v1 makes no claim about any real epithelium: no specimen is loaded or segmented, so no verdict on T1917-018 can be drawn from v1.." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add negative/ablation controls (Poisson-Voronoi null with matched vertex count, square/brick lattice with four-fold vertices, shuffled-angle null) and goodness-of-fit between the fitted-eps froth angle distribution and each specimen (Pearson r and RMSE of binned histograms, two-sample KS statistic, coefficient of variation); write datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-018/result.json with the verdict and headline numbers, and extend measure_morphoeval() with specimen-side measurements.",
            "remediation needed: Implement the equal-tension soap-froth limit (Gamma_bar = 0) with a convergence criterion and T1 edge exchanges, add the orientation-dependent line tension Lambda(phi) = Lambda0 (1 + eps cos 2 phi) of E5 and sweep eps over 0..0.6 (7 points) to show monotone angle dispersion (Fig. 124 regime); add a partition-tension-ratio sweep of E1; expose --eps, --lambda-bar, --gamma-bar, --seed, --steps and --quick CLI flags.",
            "remediation needed: Load and SHA-256-verify all four vendored specimens against reference.json; segment the cell-border network of the corneal endothelium and onion epidermis (border channel -> watershed from nucleus/centre markers) and binarise Thompson's Figs. 103 and 124; detect tri-cellular vertices from label images and measure the three interior angles per vertex by circular label sampling at a stated radius; report f3, SD, RMS deviation, median |theta-120| and fraction within the a-priori +/-15 deg tolerance per specimen, with bootstrap CIs." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.402"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (Cursor cloud agent, primary assessor)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

